Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:35:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/22] [M156] bluetooth: Bind chooser event handler with
 WeakPtr in GetDevice

Original change's description:
> bluetooth: Bind chooser event handler with WeakPtr in GetDevice
>
> In BluetoothDeviceChooserController::GetDevice(), chooser_event_handler
> was bound with base::Unretained(this) before calling
> BluetoothDelegate::RunBluetoothChooser(). If the requesting frame is
> detached while RunBluetoothChooser() drops fullscreen (before
> RunBluetoothChooser() returns and assigns chooser_),
> BluetoothDeviceChooserController is destroyed while chooser_ is still
> null, so ~BluetoothChooserDesktop() never resets the event handler. When
> ShowDeviceChooserDialog() subsequently bails out and destroys
> BluetoothChooserController, its destructor invokes event_handler_ on the
> freed BluetoothDeviceChooserController.
>
> Bind OnBluetoothChooserEvent with weak_ptr_factory_.GetWeakPtr() instead
> of base::Unretained(this), and check that callback_ has not already been
> consumed synchronously during RunBluetoothChooser() before assigning
> chooser_ and starting device discovery.
>
